From d4588f1550b57b243750e3c2d351910643bd8463 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 10:21:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Kernels: inverses of the jacobians computed once by the
 geometry kernel

The kernels only used the jacobians of the element transformations through
their inverses, computed again by each thread at each point (for each pair
of nodes in the stiffness matrices kernel): nine divisions, eighteen
multiplications and nine subtractions in double precision, slow on the GPUs
whose double precision throughput is low. The geometry kernel now computes
the inverses (same formula, invertJacobian) and stores them instead of the
jacobians (ElementsJacobians::invJ, same layout, same memory); the
gradients, inner forces, stiffness matrices, action, FBar and Faltus kernels
read them (loadInverseJacobian). The values are the same on the host, bit
for bit, and on a GPU up to the order of the atomic additions.

Assembly of the stiffness matrices on a GPU: 1.7 to 2.2 times faster in
mechanics, 5.9 times in heat transfer (56 registers instead of 84); on the
host, a few percent faster.
